[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5801676011","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123771#issuecomment-5801676011","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123771","id":5801676011,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABWc6M6w","user":{"login":"tldmbruno","id":118130235,"node_id":"U_kgDOBwqGOw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/118130235?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno","html_url":"https://github.com/tldmbruno","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-23T19:41:27Z","updated_at":"2026-09-23T19:41:27Z","body":"This may look like an extremely niche bug. My game has handheld cameras, which makes heavy use of SubViewport render target update mode ONCE (every 12 frames) for performance reasons. Then I started seeing blinking artifacts and [thought it was the Multimeshes' fault](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120005). Dug deeper and found the source of the problem. The \"blinking\" was the \"update ONCE\" being called. Switched to update ALWAYS and the true bug appeared in all its glory.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5801676011/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6017757627","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123771#issuecomment-6017757627","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123771","id":6017757627,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABZq-xuw","user":{"login":"tldmbruno","id":118130235,"node_id":"U_kgDOBwqGOw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/118130235?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno","html_url":"https://github.com/tldmbruno","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-06T13:52:23Z","updated_at":"2026-10-06T13:52:23Z","body":"Just found out that it is way easier to reproduce the bug.\n\nCompatibility or Mobile. Two cameras, 1 as a child of a SubViewport with UPDATE ALWAYS. 1 Light, and some mesh to be lit by it. Set the Light's cull mask to a layer where the main camera can't see. Two things will happen: 1) The light will render anyway. 2) The relative position of the light for the main camera will mimic the relative position of the light for the subviewport camera.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6017757627/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6018653308","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123771#issuecomment-6018653308","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123771","id":6018653308,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABZr1cfA","user":{"login":"tldmbruno","id":118130235,"node_id":"U_kgDOBwqGOw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/118130235?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno","html_url":"https://github.com/tldmbruno","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-06T14:38:23Z","updated_at":"2026-10-06T14:38:23Z","body":"Made many changes for the description and title, since I understand the bug way better now. It is a cull issue. Way less niche than I thought it was when I first discovered it.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6018653308/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6063927193","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123771#issuecomment-6063927193","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123771","id":6063927193,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABaXAvmQ","user":{"login":"tldmbruno","id":118130235,"node_id":"U_kgDOBwqGOw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/118130235?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno","html_url":"https://github.com/tldmbruno","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-08T16:02:12Z","updated_at":"2026-10-08T16:02:12Z","body":"For those struggling with the same bug: There are three workarounds.\n\n1. Put all lights in a layer the SubViewport camera cannot see. Give the camera some \"night vision goggles\" effect or use additive transparent meshes to simulate light in those layers.\n2. Increase the AABB for all lights by huge amounts, so the lights never get frustum culled. If you fear performance issues, use visibility notifiers or check the cameras' angles with a dot product function.\n3. Use Forward+.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6063927193/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]